    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just hard to see it that way. it feels like a math equation that doesn't add up. i put in two decades of my life, my energy, my soul into this... and now the balance is zero. there's no way to get that time back. it feels like i'm just operating at a massive deficit forever. like why even keep trying to build something else when the cost is always going to be higher than the reward?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes sense that you feel trapped in a deficit when the past can't be undone, but the cost of trying again is simply the price of living, not a reason to stop. You don't have to build anything new today; just acknowledge that the pain is real and that you are still here, capable of feeling it. Sometimes the only way to make the math work is to stop trying to balance the equation and just let yourself rest without guilt.",
      "source": "target",
